{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Consolas;}}{\colortbl ;\red15\green23\blue42;\red30\green58\blue138;\red14\green116\blue144;\red71\green85\blue105;\red203\green213\blue225;}\viewkind4\uc1 \paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1440\margr1440\margt1440\margb1440 \pard\qc\sa120\sb100\f0\fs28\b\cf1 CHAPTER 05\par SYSTEM DESIGN\b0\par \pard\sa160\cf5 _________________________________________________________________________________\cf1\par \pard\sa140\sb140\f0\fs24\b\cf2 5.1 Architectural Representation\b0\par \pard\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 The system architecture of the project \"Detecting Criminal Activities from CCTV Using Object Detection and Machine Learning Algorithms\" is structured into seven modular, interconnected layers designed for real-time video ingestion, deep learning computer vision inference, temporal threat validation, automated evidence generation, and role-governed human verification.\par \pard\li240\ri240\f1\fs16\cf1 +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par |                              INPUT LAYER                                |\par |  +--------------------+--------------------+-------------------------+  |\par |  | CCTV / IP Camera   | Webcam / USB       | Uploaded Video          |  |\par |  | Stream             | Camera             | Files (MP4/AVI)         |  |\par |  +--------------------+--------------------+-------------------------+  |\par +------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\par                                      |\par                                      v\par +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par |                         VIDEO PROCESSING LAYER                          |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | OpenCV Video Capture and Frame Extraction                         |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | Frame Preparation, Validation & 3.0-Second RAM Ring Buffer        |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par +------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\par                                      |\par                                      v\par +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par |                           AI DETECTION LAYER                            |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | Configured YOLO Detection Model (YOLOv8n CPU Engine)              |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | Person Detection  |  Supported Weapon Detection                   |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | Bounding Boxes  |  Class Labels  |  Confidence Scores             |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par +------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\par                                      |\par                                      v\par +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par |                        BACKEND APPLICATION LAYER                        |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | FastAPI Backend Framework (Asynchronous ASGI Uvicorn Server)      |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | Request Handling  |  Result Processing  |  API Communication      |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par +------------------+-----------------------------------+------------------+\par                    |                                   |\par                    v                                   v\par +------------------------------------+   +--------------------------------+\par |        INCIDENT MANAGEMENT         |   |          DATA STORAGE          |\par |  - Organize Detection Results      |   |  - SQLite Database (WAL Mode)  |\par |  - Review Available Threat Alerts  |   |  - SQLAlchemy Database Access  |\par +------------------+-----------------+   +-----------------+--------------+\par                    |                                       |\par                    +-------------------+-------------------+\par                                        |\par                                        v\par +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par |                           PRESENTATION LAYER                            |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | React Web Interface (Single-Page Application in TypeScript)       |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par |  | Video Display  |  Detection Results  |  Incident Information      |  |\par |  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\par +------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\par                                      |\par                                      v\par +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par |                              HUMAN REVIEW                               |\par |  Authorized User Reviews Potential Detection Alerts and Determines      |\par |  Whether Further Law Enforcement Investigation Is Needed (RBAC Gated)   |\par +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par                  Fig 5.1.1 Architectural Representation\par \pard\sa160\sb160\cf5 _________________________________________________________________________________\cf1\par \pard\sa140\sb140\f0\fs24\b\cf2 5.2 Architectural Description\b0\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 The architecture of the "Detecting Criminal Activities from CCTV" project consists of several connected components that work together to analyze video footage and display detection results. The main components include the video input module, video-processing module, AI-based object detection module, backend services, web user interface, and data storage. Each component performs a specific function, allowing the application to process video and organize potential threat alerts efficiently.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 1. Input Layer: Handles diverse video input feeds including live CCTV IP camera streams (over RTSP/TCP), USB webcams, and pre-recorded surveillance video recordings uploaded by forensic analysts for batch processing.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 2. Video Processing Layer: Powered by OpenCV (cv2.VideoCapture), this layer extracts video frames, validates input integrity, normalizes dimensions to 640x480 RGB, and maintains a rolling 3.0-second circular buffer in memory for zero-loss pre-incident evidence recording.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 3. AI Detection Layer: Implements the Ultralytics YOLOv8n deep learning network optimized for multi-core CPU execution. Employs dual model weights for person tracking and weapon detection (handguns, knives), producing normalized bounding boxes, class labels, and confidence probabilities.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 4. Backend Application Layer: Built using FastAPI and Uvicorn, handling asynchronous HTTP REST requests, client API communications, and real-time multipart/x-mixed-replace MJPEG video streaming directly to client web browsers.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 5. Incident Management: The temporal confirmation gate evaluates detections across time, firing an incident trigger only when a threat persists across consecutive frames (K >= 2). It automatically packages a 6-second MP4 evidence clip (3s pre-event + 3s post-event) and a peak-confidence JPEG thumbnail.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 6. Data Storage: An asynchronous SQLite 3 database operating in Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) mode via SQLAlchemy 2.0. WAL mode allows concurrent readers to access incident logs and camera records while workers write new evidence with zero database locking.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 7. Presentation Layer: A responsive single-page web console constructed in React 18, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. Furnishes live CCTV grid monitoring, forensic upload queues, incident review triage, and evidence playback.\par \pard\sa140\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1 8. Human Review: Serves as the supervisory governance layer enforcing Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Field Operators have monitoring clearance; Threat Analysts review, acknowledge, and triage alerts; while Lead Administrators configure hardware and AI detection thresholds.\par \par}